MATCH_BEGIN 25ee8fbd59f235f8dae299335cd60ada348ddc841e228883dc8e6665dc6c1372-docs__NegRiskOperator.md LINES 37 51
LINE 37 
LINE 38 ## `prepareQuestion`
LINE 39 
LINE 40 Proxies the NegRisk `prepareQuestion` function.
LINE 41 
LINE 42 RequestIds are provided which link an oracle request to the specific question. For NegRisk questions, requestIds always differ from questionIds, and the request must be made specifically _before_ the question is prepared.
LINE 43 
LINE 44 If the requestId has already been used for some question, the function will revert.
LINE 45 
LINE 46 ### Parameters
LINE 47 
LINE 48 ```[solidity]
LINE 49 bytes32 _marketId
LINE 50 bytes _data
LINE 51 bytes32 _requestId
MATCH_END
MATCH_BEGIN 25ee8fbd59f235f8dae299335cd60ada348ddc841e228883dc8e6665dc6c1372-docs__NegRiskOperator.md LINES 51 65
LINE 51 bytes32 _requestId
LINE 52 ```
LINE 53 
LINE 54 ## `resolveQuestion`
LINE 55 
LINE 56 Resolves a question on the NegRiskAdapter once the oracle has reported the outcome via `reportPayouts`.
LINE 57 
LINE 58 There is a one hour delay period which must elapse between the call to `reportPayouts` and the call to `resolveQuestion`. This serves as a safety period in case there is a manipulation of the oracle.
LINE 59 
LINE 60 ## `reportPayouts`
LINE 61 
LINE 62 Receives the result of a question from the oracle. The oracle is expected to respond with a length two array of uint256s, `[1,0]` if yes, `[0,1]` if no. No other payouts are considered valid.
LINE 63 
LINE 64 ### Parameters
LINE 65 
MATCH_END
