MATCH_BEGIN 60159f20d834ddc00080c7ed444a9705d3a9bf8f4a8635b485d2107a8a48a302-README.md LINES 13 27
LINE 13 
LINE 14 The Vault holds USDC and Yes tokens which are collected as fees from users who choose to convert NO positions, given a positive fee rate.
LINE 15 
LINE 16 ## Use with the UmaCtfAdapter
LINE 17 
LINE 18 The NegRiskOperator and NegRiskAdapter are designed to be used with the [UmaCtfAdapter](https://github.com/Polymarket/uma-ctf-adapter), or any oracle with the same interface.
LINE 19 A dedicated UmaCtfAdapter will need to be deployed with the UmaCtfAdapter's `ctf` set to the address of the NegRiskAdapter, and the NegRiskOperator's `oracle` set to the address of the UmaCtfAdapter.
LINE 20 
LINE 21 In order to prepare a question for a market using the NegRiskOperator, the question must be initialized on the UmaCtfAdapter first. Then, the question may be prepared on the NegRiskOperator where the `_requestId` parameter is the `questionID` returned by the UmaCtfAdapter.
LINE 22 
LINE 23 Note that the UmaCtfAdapter can return `[1,1]` as a possible outcome, which is not a valid outcome for the NegRiskAdapter. The NegRiskAdapter will revert if it receives this outcome. It is important that markets/questions are chosen carefully so that this outcome is not possible.
LINE 24 
LINE 25 ## Questions
LINE 26 
LINE 27 It is vital that markets prepared on the NegRiskAdapter never result in a tie or will be unable to be determined. For any given market, once one question is resolved as Yes/True, all other questions must be resolved as No/False. This means that if the chosen oracle returns a second question as Yes/True, the call to `reportOutcome` will revert, and the market may not be able to fully resolved. Similarly, it is expected that one question will resolve to Yes/True, and it should not be the case that all questions for a given market resolve to No/False. Keep this in mind when preparing markets and questions on the NegRiskAdapter.
MATCH_END
MATCH_BEGIN 60159f20d834ddc00080c7ed444a9705d3a9bf8f4a8635b485d2107a8a48a302-README.md LINES 14 27
LINE 14 The Vault holds USDC and Yes tokens which are collected as fees from users who choose to convert NO positions, given a positive fee rate.
LINE 15 
LINE 16 ## Use with the UmaCtfAdapter
LINE 17 
LINE 18 The NegRiskOperator and NegRiskAdapter are designed to be used with the [UmaCtfAdapter](https://github.com/Polymarket/uma-ctf-adapter), or any oracle with the same interface.
LINE 19 A dedicated UmaCtfAdapter will need to be deployed with the UmaCtfAdapter's `ctf` set to the address of the NegRiskAdapter, and the NegRiskOperator's `oracle` set to the address of the UmaCtfAdapter.
LINE 20 
LINE 21 In order to prepare a question for a market using the NegRiskOperator, the question must be initialized on the UmaCtfAdapter first. Then, the question may be prepared on the NegRiskOperator where the `_requestId` parameter is the `questionID` returned by the UmaCtfAdapter.
LINE 22 
LINE 23 Note that the UmaCtfAdapter can return `[1,1]` as a possible outcome, which is not a valid outcome for the NegRiskAdapter. The NegRiskAdapter will revert if it receives this outcome. It is important that markets/questions are chosen carefully so that this outcome is not possible.
LINE 24 
LINE 25 ## Questions
LINE 26 
LINE 27 It is vital that markets prepared on the NegRiskAdapter never result in a tie or will be unable to be determined. For any given market, once one question is resolved as Yes/True, all other questions must be resolved as No/False. This means that if the chosen oracle returns a second question as Yes/True, the call to `reportOutcome` will revert, and the market may not be able to fully resolved. Similarly, it is expected that one question will resolve to Yes/True, and it should not be the case that all questions for a given market resolve to No/False. Keep this in mind when preparing markets and questions on the NegRiskAdapter.
MATCH_END
